  ],
  "slug": "amino-acid-6d41",
  "summary": "New work couples model-based gene discovery with shared databases and reproducible workflows for mobile elements, prophages, and pathogen genomics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is extracting functional gene content from microbial genomes and metagenomes at scale. A protein language model with ensemble learning identifies over 46,000 putative environmental beta-lactamases, with inverse folding used to examine mutational potential. Non-negative matrix factorization of 1,398 S. aureus genomes splits the accessory pangenome into 24 additive gene modules separating lineage from adaptation and virulence. Infrastructure items complement these methods: proMGE2 catalogues over 16.4 million mobile genetic elements across isolates and MAGs, PHI provides a Galaxy workflow for prophage identification, host prediction and annotation with standardized reporting, and gcPathogen 2.0 expands a multi-omics surveillance database. Only the first two items involve a modeling component; the rest are resources and workflows.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-16"
}
